Project: Django. Upgrade: 3.2 -> 4.2. Release of these items: 4.0.
Source: Django 4.0 release notes.

Label every item:
- risk = the change could break an application or deployment, require migration work, or create operational risk for SOME user upgrading across this release (removed or renamed APIs/settings/flags, changed defaults, behavior changes, raised minimum versions of runtimes/databases/dependencies, data or schema migration, required config changes, deprecated-and-removed features).
- context = accurate and useful but needs no user action at this release: explicitly "no user action required", a deprecation that still works (warning only), a purely additive new feature or option, documentation pointers.
- noise = credits, install/download commands, pure bug fixes that cannot change correct behavior, marketing text, headings with no content.

Return one label per item_id with a one-sentence reason grounded in the item text.

Items (JSON lines):
{"item_id": "c9eae58a14c2", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "Calling FileSystemStorage.delete() with an empty name now raises ValueError instead of AssertionError."}
{"item_id": "e86e42c784c5", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "Calling EmailMultiAlternatives.attach_alternative() or EmailMessage.attach() with an invalid content or mimetype arguments now raise ValueError instead of AssertionError."}
{"item_id": "dfca481dc28f", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "assertHTMLEqual no longer considers a non-boolean attribute without a value equal to an attribute with the same name and value."}
{"item_id": "65c12951201f", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "Tests that fail to load, for example due to syntax errors, now always match when using test --tag."}
{"item_id": "2dbc0204e52f", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented django.contrib.admin.utils.lookup_needs_distinct() function is renamed to lookup_spawns_duplicates()."}
{"item_id": "ea54056947f4", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented HttpRequest.get_raw_uri() method is removed. The HttpRequest.build_absolute_uri method may be a suitable alternative."}
{"item_id": "6842e786aaa5", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The object argument of undocumented ModelAdmin.log_addition(), log_change(), and log_deletion() methods is renamed to obj."}
{"item_id": "5d164bc7e834", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "RssFeed, Atom1Feed, and their subclasses now emit elements with no content as self-closing tags."}
{"item_id": "4393f3191df4", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "NodeList.render() no longer casts the output of render() method for individual nodes to a string. Node.render() should always return a string as documented."}
{"item_id": "4f922a1b5ac8", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The where_class property of django.db.models.sql.query.Query and the where_class argument to the private get_extra_restriction() method of ForeignObject and ForeignObjectRel are removed. If needed, initialize django.db.models.sql.where.WhereNode instead."}
{"item_id": "e7a06ac1ccaf", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The filter_clause argument of the undocumented Query.add_filter() method is replaced by two positional arguments filter_lhs and filter_rhs."}
{"item_id": "81f26f55fc1a", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "CsrfViewMiddleware now uses request.META['CSRF_COOKIE_NEEDS_UPDATE'] in place of request.META['CSRF_COOKIE_USED'], request.csrf_cookie_needs_reset, and response.csrf_cookie_set to track whether the CSRF cookie should be sent. This is an undocumented, private API."}
{"item_id": "71a49b206e18", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The undocumented TRANSLATOR_COMMENT_MARK constant is moved from django.template.base to django.utils.translation.template."}
{"item_id": "e31bd221b8de", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The real_apps argument of the undocumented django.db.migrations.state.ProjectState.init() method must now be a set if provided."}
{"item_id": "82c4486609ce", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "RadioSelect and CheckboxSelectMultiple widgets are now rendered in <div> tags so they are announced more concisely by screen readers. If you need the previous behavior, override the widget template with the appropriate template from Django 3.2."}
{"item_id": "553c4c461adf", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The floatformat template filter no longer depends on the USE_L10N setting and always returns localized output. Use the u suffix to disable localization."}
{"item_id": "40019b0edc1b", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The default value of the USE_L10N setting is changed to True. See the Localization section above for more details."}
{"item_id": "e127992a6fb1", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "As part of the move to zoneinfo, django.utils.timezone.utc is changed to alias datetime.timezone.utc."}
{"item_id": "55be8262b4b7", "section": "Django 4.0 release notes / Backwards incompatible changes in 4.0 / Miscellaneous", "text": "The minimum supported version of asgiref is increased from 3.3.2 to 3.4.1."}
